dot-sync(1) -- Sync managed dotfiles
====================================

## SYNOPSIS

`dot sync` [-h] [<file>...]

## DESCRIPTION

Sync one or more managed dotfiles from the dotfile repository. See the ENVIRONMENT section of dot(1) for details.

"Syncing" means linking, re-linking, or fixing broken links of dotfiles.
- If the dotfile is not present, link it.
- If the dotfile _is_ present, remove and re-link it, regardless of where it's linked to.

Part of dot(1).

## OPTIONS

  * `-h`, `--h`:
    Show command help.

  * [<file>]:
    One or more managed files (optional). Paths are relative to the dotfile repo. If no files are passed, all managed files will be synced.
